</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Unit Tests</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To quantify the immediate executability of generated code without manual modification, we conducted systematic unit testing on a representative sample of 20 code implementations produced by our highest-performing architecture (<math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=4</annotation></semantics></math> refinements) that successfully passed both keyword filtering and <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">LLM</abbr> jury assessments. Unit test generation employed GPT-o3 through OpenAI’s interface, producing comprehensive test suites for each code sample. All testing procedures utilized Python execution environments, generating 160 individual unit tests across the 20-code evaluation set (average of 8 tests per code sample).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Unit testing results.</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
